# (see fixture/ for the pages added to it); swap them for your own content
# when you copy a feature.
Feature: Home page
  As a visitor
  I want the home page to render and hydrate correctly
  So that I know the Gatsby production build works

  Background:
    Given I am on the homepage

  Scenario: The home page is a Gatsby production build
    Then the page should be generated by Gatsby
    And the page should be generated by Gatsby version "5"
    And the site should be a production build
    And the page should be from the current build

  Scenario: The home page is rendered and hydrated
    Then the page title should be "Home | Gatsby Default Starter"
    And I should see "Welcome to Gatsby!"
    And I should see a hydrated page
    And there should be no hydration errors
    And there should be no JavaScript errors

  Scenario: The home page content is in the HTML without JavaScript
    Then I should see "Welcome to Gatsby!" without JavaScript
    And I should not see "Rendered in the browser" without JavaScript

  Scenario: The home page head is written by the Head API
    Then the page head should be set by the Head API
    And the meta tag should exist with the following attributes:
      | name        | description |
    And the web app manifest should be valid

  Scenario: The home page has an optimized image
    Then I should see an optimized image
    And the optimized image should be loaded
    And the optimized image should have a placeholder
    And the optimized image should offer the "avif" format
    And the optimized image should offer the "webp" format

  Scenario: The home page data was built
    Then the page-data for "/" should be available
    And the page-data for "/page-2/" should be available
    And the page-data for "/no-such-page/" should not be available

  Scenario: Links in the viewport are prefetched
    Given I should see a hydrated page
    Then the page "/page-2/" should be prefetched
    And the page "/using-typescript/" should be prefetched
